{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q419806","formula":"CeCl₃","hill":"CeCl3","elements":["Cl","Ce"],"composition":{"Ce":1.0,"Cl":3.0},"names":{"en":"Cerous chloride","ru":"Хлорид церия(III)"},"descriptions":{"en":"Cerium(III) chloride (CeCl3), also known as cerous chloride or cerium trichloride, is a compound of cerium and chlorine. It is a white hygroscopic salt; it rapidly absorbs water to form hydrates, which may be of variable composition.The hexa- and heptahydrate CeCl3·7H2O are known. All forms are highly soluble in water, and the anhydrous derivative is soluble in ethanol and acetone.","ru":"Хлорид церия(III) — бинарное неорганическое соединение, соль металла церия и соляной кислоты с формулой CeCl3, бесцветные кристаллы, растворимые в воде, образует кристаллогидрат."},"fame":22,"pubchemCid":24636,"mass":246.47,"charge":0,"smiles":"[Cl-].[Cl-].[Cl-].[Ce+3]","inchikey":"VYLVYHXQOHJDJL-UHFFFAOYSA-K","iupac":"cerium(3+) trichloride","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-582011","atoms":8,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[7.505,0.0,0.0],[-3.752,6.499,0.0],[0.0,0.0,4.298]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":3.752,"y":2.166,"z":3.224,"el":"Ce"},{"x":0.0,"y":4.333,"z":1.075,"el":"Ce"},{"x":4.57,"y":3.973,"z":1.075,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-0.818,"y":2.526,"z":3.224,"el":"Cl"},{"x":1.973,"y":4.528,"z":3.224,"el":"Cl"},{"x":1.779,"y":1.971,"z":1.075,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-1.156,"y":5.944,"z":3.224,"el":"Cl"},{"x":4.908,"y":0.555,"z":1.075,"el":"Cl"}],"bonds":[[0,5,1],[1,6,1],[0,7,1],[1,4,1],[0,2,1],[1,3,1],[0,4,1],[1,5,1]],"cellOrigin":[0,0,0]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q419806","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cerium%28III%29_chloride","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"r